    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec: on a successful owner create, emit an audit line via the logger named `AUDIT` containing the owner id, the `customerCode`, and the `registrationDate`.\n\nI implemented it as a new cohesive pipeline step rather than modifying any existing function \u2014 keeping structural impact minimal (the only function I authored has zero surrounding class complexity, and no existing method grew):\n\n1. **New function** `AuditOwnerCreated.java` \u2014 a single-method step that reads the persisted `@Val Owner` and logs `owner created id=\u2026 customerCode=\u2026 registrationDate=\u2026` to `LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"AUDIT\")`.\n\n2. **Wired into `owners.POST.yml`** between `save` (where the id is assigned) and `respond`, under the same `transaction` governance as its neighbors, so it runs only on the success path after persistence.\n\nThe audit line appears exactly once on create (`INFO AUDIT - owner created id=11 customerCode=TOW-SUR-0001 registrationDate=2026-09-02`), and `AcceptanceTest.coreLogsAuditOnCreate` plus the full suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
